Local Data Handling:
  Use local mock data for components until a backend server is implemented.
  Consider using json-server for simulating backend API calls during development.
User Role Management:
  Implement role-based routing to separate interfaces for patients and orthopedists.
  Ensure that the orthopedist interface has access to additional pages and advanced analytics features.
Responsive Design:
  Design the application to be mobile-first for patients, ensuring optimal usability on mobile devices.
  Create an adapted web version for orthopedists, focusing on a desktop-friendly layout and functionality.
Component Structure:
  Organize components to accommodate both mobile and web interfaces, possibly using conditional rendering or separate components for each platform.
  Ensure that shared components are reusable and maintainable across both interfaces.
Performance Optimization:

  Optimize the application for performance on both mobile and web platforms, considering the different capabilities of devices used by patients and orthopedists